# Next.js App Rules

## Router awareness
- Detect which router this repo uses before writing routing code: `app/` directory → App Router; `pages/` → Pages Router. Match the existing one — do not mix.
- **App Router**: Server Components by default; `'use client'` only at the leaves that need interactivity. Data fetching in Server Components or Route Handlers, not `getServerSideProps`.
- **Pages Router**: data fetching via `getServerSideProps` / `getStaticProps`; no Server Components.

## Project layout
- Routes in `app/` or `pages/`; shared UI in `components/`; server-only code never imported from client components.
- API routes (`app/api/` or `pages/api/`) are thin: validate input, call a service/lib function, shape the response.

## Data & rendering
- Choose the rendering mode per route deliberately (static / SSR / ISR / client) and be able to say why. Default to static when data allows.
- Use `next/image` and `next/font` instead of raw `<img>` / CSS font-face when available.
- Environment variables: `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` is client-visible — never put secrets in it.

## Testing
- Match the repo's runner (Vitest or Jest) + React Testing Library for components.
- Mock the router with the repo's existing helper; do not hand-roll router mocks per test.
